  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ReACCION Protection for Human Rights Defenders Human Rights Defenders - Institute for International Education (IIE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central America Regional):  Through the Centroamerica en Ascenso program, this activity will provide medium-term protection opportunities for study at U.S. higher education institutions (HEIs) to anti-corruption champions and democracy activists to continue their work from a safe location. Through this activity USAID will: 1) award human rights defenders from Central America one to two-year fellowships at host HEIs in the United States; 2) enable fellows to strengthen skills, learn and grow professionally, and expand their networks; 3) support fellows to expand their work to counter corruption towards advancing democracy and promoting human rights. The implementing partner has wide experience implementing fellowship programs for emerging leaders in at-risk environments.The Fellowship Program will identify and support approximately 35 individuals-including but not limited to jurists, judges, journalists, rights defenders, activists, and civil society members-working to counter corruption, protect civic space, and promote democratic values. With FY 2024 funds, the activity will complete recruitment, placement, and ongoing mentorship of approximately 15 Fellows in higher education institutions in the United States, including American University,the University of Notre Dame, and the University of Florida. The activity will also support integration into broader USG anti-corruption efforts in northern Central America, and facilitate research projects in conjunction with local civil society organizations, advocating for greater transparency.  The activity will contribute to RDO 2 and support Pillar II RCS by supporting anti-corruption champions to continue to grow and expand their work even from outside their countries. It will also advance Pillars III and V of the U.S. Strategy on Countering Corruption.</narrative>
  </description>
